# Mutation routes with NO AUTHORIZATION DEPENDENCY — frozen baseline.
#
# Generated by gdx_dispatch/tests/authz_sweep.py (unpermissioned_mutations),
# enforced by gdx_dispatch/tests/test_authz_permission_sweep.py. A RATCHET, not
# an approval list: every line was already here on 2026-09-09, and CI fails when
# a NEW one appears.
#
# The sibling ratchet (.authz_ungated_baseline) asks "is anyone there?".
# This one asks "are they allowed?" — a route carrying only `get_current_user`
# scored identically to one carrying `require_permission(...)` until the
# dependency set was split apart.
#
# ⚠ A LINE HERE IS NOT PROOF OF A HOLE. The sweep reads dependencies plus a
# text heuristic over the handler body; a gate reached through a helper, or an
# ownership check on the record itself, is invisible to it. Read the handler
# before calling any line a defect.
#
# Removing a line is the goal:
#   from gdx_dispatch.core.modules import require_permission   # NOT core.permissions
#   dependencies=[Depends(require_permission("invoices.write"))]
# Keys are catalogued in gdx_dispatch/core/permissions.py (61 of them).
#
# ⚠ Check who loses access FIRST. The gate 403s every user whose role snapshot
# lacks the key. Only admin and owner pass via the BUILTIN union escape hatch.
#
# Counts at freeze: 405 total — 392 staff, 13 customer-portal.
#
# 371 → 370 (2026-09-27, GDXA-90): pruned POST /portal/invoices/{invoice_id}/pay.
# DELETED, not gated — routers/portal.py:644 records the removal (2026-09-16):
# nothing called it, and a second card-mint site that could not carry the card
# surcharge would have breached the networks' surcharge-consistency rule.
#
# 370 → 372 (2026-09-28, planner Today tab): PUT /api/planner/tasks/{task_id}/today
# and PUT /api/planner/today/note. ADDED, deliberately open to any authenticated
# staff user of the jobs module — like every other /api/planner mutation listed
# below, and there is no planner permission key to gate on. Each acts only on the
# caller's own records: the pin refuses a task outside the caller's own set
# (services/planner_today.py NotYours → 403) and the note is keyed to the
# caller's user id. See the 2026-09-28 planner Today plan.
# 372 → 374 (2026-09-28, text an invoice): POST /api/mobile/invoices/{invoice_id}/
# send-sms and /sms-preview. ADDED, same shape as the /send and /send-receipt
# lines beside them: a technician holds no invoices permission, so these are
# authorized in the handler — the invoice must be on the caller's own job
# (_tech_owned_invoice → 403), office-verified (409), and phone_com enabled.
# 374 → 376 (2026-09-29, text an estimate): POST /api/mobile/quotes/{estimate_id}/
# send-sms and /sms-preview. ADDED, same shape as the /accept and /decline
# lines beside them: techs do not hold estimates.send (docs/tech_mobile.md), so
# these are authorized in the handler — the quote must sit on a job assigned
# to the caller via the shared core/job_access gate (_tech_textable_quote →
# 403; a quote with no job is refused) and phone_com must be enabled.
# 376 → 380 (2026-09-30, scheduled texts): POST /api/mobile/invoices/{invoice_id}/
# schedule-sms and /api/mobile/quotes/{estimate_id}/schedule-sms — ADDED, the
# same handler gates as their /send-sms twins above (_mobile_sms_invoice +
# office verification; _tech_textable_quote). POST /api/phone-com/messages/
# schedule and /api/phone-com/scheduled/{scheduled_id}/cancel — ADDED, the same
# gate as POST /api/phone-com/messages (the phone_com module; any staff user
# who can reply can reply later, and cancel a text not yet sending). Every
# scheduled text is re-judged when it fires: the scheduler must still be an
# active user, and an office invoice/estimate text still needs invoices.send /
# estimates.send (modules/phone_com/scheduled.py). Plan:
# docs/design/scheduled-sms-plan.md.
#
# 380 → 381 (2026-10-06, multi-day jobs PR 3): POST /api/jobs/{job_id}/day-close —
# ADDED, the same handler gate as its sibling POST /api/jobs/{job_id}/closeout
# below: core/job_access.job_write_denial (the jobs write key AND a claim on the
# job — assignment, visit or crew row — or office tier). The sweep cannot see a
# gate reached through that helper. Plan: multi-day jobs plan §5.4a.
#
# 381 → 383 (2026-10-07, portal quote request): POST /portal/quote-requests and
# /portal/quote-requests/{request_id}/photos — ADDED, customer-portal routes
# like their neighbours below. Ownership is in the handler: the request is
# created for principal.customer_id, and a photo is refused (404) unless the
# request's customer_id is the caller's (test_portal_quote_requests.py,
# test_a_customer_sees_only_their_own_requests). Plan:
# docs/design/portal-quote-request-plan.md.
#
# 383 → 385 (2026-10-07, same plan): PATCH /portal/quote-requests/{request_id}
# and POST /portal/quote-requests/{request_id}/withdraw — the customer changing
# or withdrawing their own request. Same ownership check (_own_request_or_404,
# 404 for another customer's id: test_another_customer_can_neither_edit_nor_withdraw).
#
# 385 → 389 (2026-10-08, contractor resale quotes): PUT /portal/reseller/profile,
# POST /portal/reseller/logo, POST /portal/estimates/{estimate_id}/resale and
# DELETE /portal/resale-quotes/{quote_id} — a contractor or wholesale portal
# customer's own branding and resale quotes. The gate is in the handler:
# pricing_class must be contractor/wholesale (403 otherwise), the current
# disclaimer must be accepted (403), the estimate must be the caller's and
# customer-visible (_get_customer_estimate_or_404), and a quote is refused
# (404) unless its customer_id is the caller's (_own_quote_or_404;
# test_portal_resale.py, test_customer_b_cannot_read_or_delete_customer_as_quote).
# Plan: docs/design/contractor-resale-quotes-plan.md.
#
# 389 → 390 (2026-10-09, GDXA-375 job cancel lifecycle): POST /api/jobs/{job_id}/cancel —
# ADDED, the same handler gate as its siblings POST /api/jobs/{job_id}/reactivate
# and /uncomplete below: core/job_access.job_write_denial (the jobs write key AND
# a claim on the job, or office tier). The sweep cannot see a gate reached
# through that helper.

